     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nTypical adult oral regimens are:\n- **Mild to moderate pain or fever:** 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Inflammatory conditions or higher analgesic need:** 600\u2013800 mg three or four times daily. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and the lowest effective dose is preferred.\n\nPlease confirm what you intended. For example, you may have meant 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 400 mg four times daily. If 1,600 mg per dose really is what you want, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
